From 504a961c5963db2fce0f5028faafb67b7b99746e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:55:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: missing-parent repair grant forwards only
 its own child; document the release-event invariant

Follow-up to reviews 5889436348, 5889810989 and 5890066480 on PR #1945 (card t_01a1d473c3268cce):

1. The docstrings on missing_parent_repair_grant and current_block_payload said the
   failure breaker re-holds a card as `blocked` with only a gave_up event. The real trip
   (kanban_failure_accounting._record_task_failure) lands it in `triage`, which the
   status check already refuses. The gave_up arm is now described as defence in depth,
   and test_real_breaker_trip_after_a_release_leaves_no_grant drives the real breaker.
2. The release events are a named constant, BLOCK_RELEASE_EVENTS, with the invariant
   both this grant and kanban_operator_call._agent_block rely on: every write that puts a
   card into `blocked` appends a `blocked` event; a path that re-holds without one must
   append one or list the kind it left `blocked` with. It now also lists `promoted` (the
   readiness pass leaves `blocked` with no `unblocked`) and `promoted_manual`
   (`hermes kanban promote` from blocked). RED: the manually-promoted and
   readiness-promoted cases of test_hold_placed_after_the_parent_missing_block_stays_refused
   granted a release of the re-held child on the old constant.
3. _forward_missing_parent_unblock forwarded when the repair card's creator was unknown
   (None). It now forwards only when the creator is the target; otherwise the worker gets
   the plain local refusal. The detector always records creator_task_id, and Board-synced
   copies carry the created event's payload. RED: the creator-unknown case fails on the
   old `not in (None, tid)` check.
4. test_worker_kanban_unblock_tool_forwards_to_the_home_end_to_end calls the real
   kanban_unblock tool on the worker gateway of the two-gateway fixture (no stub on
   kfc.refusal or handle_supervisor_request) and asserts the hub applies the unblock
   attributed to the repair card.
5. The kanban_unblock tool's missing-parent branch now writes the same audit row as the
   self-heal and owner-wake grants (`missing_parent_requeue` {by, repair_card, target}).
   RED: test_repair_worker_unblocks_its_child_attributed_to_the_repair_card.
